			"text": "!! Basic Usage
The drawers plugin puts at both sides of the page two sliding drawers with one or several tabs, each holding a tiddler — be it one of TW's standard tiddlers or the tiddler constructed by the user to address their specific needs.

In default setup the right drawer holds the sidebar (`$:/core/ui/PageTemplate/sidebar`) and the left one hold each of the sidebar tabs (Open/Recent/Tools/More) seperately.

The visibility, content and width of the drawers, as well as their optional blurry backdrops can be set in ControlPanel > Appearance > Drawers. There is also an option to automatically close the drawer when navigating to a tidder in a StoryRiver.

!! Styling The Drawers
Additional classes to be applied to the drawers are contained in $:/plugins/euth/drawers/config/leftClass and $:/plugins/euth/drawers/config/rightClass . By default they are set to `tc-sidebar-header tc-sidebar-lists` to style the drawers just like the native sidebar.

@@.tc-muted ToDo: add examples for styling the drawers and their contents, as the selectors can be tricky. @@

!! Drawer Contents
The contents of the drawer can be defined as a simple title list (with &#91;&#91;double square brackets&#93;&#93; enclosing titles with spaces), or as a filter, which allows to implement more sophisticated logic.

@@.tc-muted ToDo: examples? @@

!! Setting Tab Captions
The label on the drawer's tab is determined either by the tiddlers title, or by its `caption` field, when it's present. The user can set the caption to display arbitrary text, icons or whatever they like. 

But sometimes it is undesirable to modify the tiddler (e.g. when it is a system tiddler) and its title is too long to fit in a tab — then $:/plugins/euth/drawers/captionsDictionary comes into play. It is a JSON data tiddler containing name/value pairs, where the name is a tiddler's title and the value is a caption to be assigned to it (don't forget to escape the quotation marks with a backslach: `\"`). 

In default setup it is used to display a flipping chevron as a sidebar handle.",
